config.profiles:
Commands offered by the `⌄` dropdown next to `+` in the Tmux view's toolbar. Each profile runs as the tmux session's own process, so quitting it ends the session.

These are merged over the built-in profiles (`Claude Code`, `Codex`, `Gemini`, `Cursor`, `Grok`). Set a key to `null` to hide a built-in one, or add your own key to define a new profile:

```json
"tmuxOpener.profiles": {
  "Gemini": null,
  "Claude Code": { "command": "claude --continue" },
  "Build": { "command": "npm run watch", "sessionSuffix": "build" }
}
```

Overriding a built-in profile replaces all of its fields, so a partial override (e.g. only `command`) drops the built-in's other defaults such as `updateCommand`.
